description:
Craft a prompt that makes Claude rewrite this JavaScript function as a one-line arrow function:

```javascript
function double(x) {
  return x * 2;
}
```
Claude must use an implicit return (no curly braces, no return keyword).

Find and fix the bug. Write a prompt that makes Claude identify why this crashes and provide a safe version:

```javascript
function getUserCity(user) {
  return user.address.city;
}
```
The fix must handle the case where `user` or `user.address` is null/undefined.

Write a prompt that gets Claude to analyze the time complexity of this code AND suggest a more efficient version:

```python
def find_duplicate(lst):
    for i in range(len(lst)):
        for j in range(len(lst)):
            if i != j and lst[i] == lst[j]:
                return lst[i]
    return None
```
